---
/**
 * THE BRAND LOCKUP. Single source of truth for the wordmark + tagline.
 *
 * THE LOCKUP IS A VECTOR IMAGE, NOT LIVE TEXT (Antonio's decision "B",
 * 2026-08-03). The full story lives in scripts/gen-lockup.py, which
 * generates brand-lockup.svg; short version: live text is painted by each
 * visitor's font engine, macOS and Linux round glyph advances differently,
 * and after three generations of alignment work the last device pixel still
 * wobbled between his screen and the build's. Outlines rasterise identically
 * everywhere, so the D-under-S and E-under-G alignment is now a mathematical
 * property of the asset, not a rendering outcome.
 *
 * TO CHANGE THE LETTERING, TAGLINE, WEIGHTS OR COLOURS:
 *   edit scripts/gen-lockup.py, run  python3 scripts/gen-lockup.py,
 *   commit the regenerated SVG. Do NOT hand-edit the SVG.
 *
 * The widths below are exact by construction: the SVG viewBox is trimmed to
 * the ink, and width = (ink-width em ratio 6.7390) x the wordmark font size
 * each variant used as text. So the lockup renders at precisely the sizes
 * Antonio approved, on every screen.
 *
 * TWO VARIANTS, TWO WIDTH REFERENCES, still deliberate:
 *   full    the site header AND the rescue tunnel bar
 *   footer  sized to the SOCIAL ROW (his rectangle rule: wordmark, tagline
 *           and social row are ONE width; change the social buttons and the
 *           footer sizes here must be re-derived)
 * Accessibility: the SVG carries role="img" and an aria-label with the full
 * brand line, so assistive tech reads words, not paths.
 */
import lockup from './brand-lockup.svg?raw';

interface Props {
  variant?: 'full' | 'footer';
}
const { variant = 'full' } = Astro.props;
const cls = variant === 'footer' ? 'smg-foot' : 'smg-full';
---
<span class:list={['smg-brand', cls]} set:html={lockup} />

<style is:global>
  .smg-brand { display: block; line-height: 0; }
  .smg-brand svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }

  /* width = 6.7390 x the wordmark font-size each variant used as live text,
     so nothing moved visually in the conversion. */
  .smg-full { width: 9.4009rem; }            /* 1.395rem word */
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .smg-full { width: 11.0250rem; } }  /* 1.636rem */
  @media (max-width: 400px) { .smg-full { width: 8.9763rem; } }   /* 1.332rem */

  .smg-foot { width: 10.8161rem; }           /* 1.605rem word */
  @media (max-width: 414px) { .smg-foot { width: 8.9696rem; } }   /* 1.331rem */
</style>
